It was my second Saturday in the little café.
I had already learned to use the machine.
A woman was sitting at the fifth table in the corner.
She waved at me.
I walked over to her to take her order.
"I would like a ginger beer," she said.
"Of course," I answered with a smile.
I walked back behind the counter.
I had not served a ginger beer before.
I looked into the large glass fridge.
I could only see regular soda and juice.
I crouched down to see the bottom shelf.
It was a bit hard to see anything.
I moved some large boxes to look behind them.
I dug around a bit right down at the bottom.
Finally, I found what I was looking for.
There stood a cold bottle of ginger beer.
I took it out of the glass fridge.
Now I had learned to find it.
I walked back to the fifth table and gave the woman the bottle.
